{
  "name": "scene-a",
  "notes": [
    "Scene A rebuild (Tony, plan R2 wave 2; research/sprint-0930/scene-a/CHECKS.md). Runs after variant-v2 and before love, so the beat numbers below are the post-v2 ones and love.json's rooftop:8 is the merged beat.",
    "Rooftop after this pack: 0 goal card | 1 establishing (bg only, the stamp once) | 2 she is there | 3 handout (her bento = the choice) | 4 insert: whole box | 5 extreme close-up: the piece in chopsticks | 6 POV: you eat | 7 cutaway: her eyes | 8 one box, two steps: 'Sweet. Like me.' then 'Sweet, ne?' (peek) | 9 'Don't stare' + the smile tag (+1) | 10 forecast, split at f-OR-ecast (she laughs) | 11 stay forever (close).",
    "props.cut = the Scene A camera + chrome (SCENES.md). Every beat sets its own cut, because props carry forward inside a scene.",
    "Voice: line texts kept so the takes match (rooftop 001, 005/006 as the lead, 007/008, 009, 010, 012, 013...). 'Sour, ne?' became 'Sour, neee?' to match take 007 as recorded. New lines (Itadakimasu, the eyes cutaway, 'Her shoes by the fence') are MC / narration: no take.",
    "yum = what you said about her cooking (best | good | salty). Only the 'Don't stare' beat reads it (vary), so each answer gets its own recorded line on that beat and the smile tag after it.",
    "nearblur: props.near = 'fence' (fx/NearLens.jsx: chain-link at the lower corners, watched from behind the fence) on the establishing beats 0-2; beat 3 (the bento handout) stops it, so the choice beats stay clean."
  ],
